{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Hi there, I'm Dr.",
   "start": 0.14,
   "end": 1.66
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Victor Petrov. Before we get going, can you tell me your full name and date of birth?",
   "start": 1.94,
   "end": 6.94
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Rodrigo Esquivel, January 30, 1982. Thanks, Rodrigo.",
   "start": 8.26,
   "end": 12.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And is your address still the one on Kellogg Avenue?",
   "start": 13.62,
   "end": 16.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, we moved in July. It's 905 Magnolia Terrace now. Got it, I'll update that.",
   "start": 16.74,
   "end": 23.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "So, Dr. Lindqvist sent you to us about your blood pressure. What's the story?",
   "start": 23.76,
   "end": 28.34
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "So, at my physical in July it was high,",
   "start": 29.02,
   "end": 31.88
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "like 156 over 98.",
   "start": 32.18,
   "end": 34.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "She had me check it at home, and it's been running in the 150s",
   "start": 34.96,
   "end": 38.68
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "over 90s pretty much every day for two months.",
   "start": 38.68,
   "end": 41.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "And she started a medicine. Yeah, amlodipine 5 mg once a day. About 6 weeks ago. It came down a little, but my readings are still like 145 over 92.",
   "start": 42.12,
   "end": 53.69
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "too.",
   "start": 53.69,
   "end": 53.85
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Any headaches,",
   "start": 54.87,
   "end": 55.41
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "vision changes, or chest pain.",
   "start": 55.87,
   "end": 57.69
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No headaches, visions fine, no chest pain.",
   "start": 58.66,
   "end": 60.98
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Shortness of breath or swelling in your legs.",
   "start": 61.66,
   "end": 63.74
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No neither.",
   "start": 64.8,
   "end": 65.32
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Dr. Lindfist wrote that you're worried because of your family. Tell me about that.",
   "start": 66.34,
   "end": 70.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, that's honestly why I'm here. My dad had a heart attack at 51 and he passed away from a second one at 58, and my mom had a stroke when she was 70, so I'm kind of freaking out about this.",
   "start": 71.28,
   "end": 83.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'm sorry about your dad. That's a real reason to take this seriously and we will. Have you ever had any heart problems yourself? Any chest pain or a heart test?",
   "start": 83.22,
   "end": 94.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No nothing, never had any heart issue, just the blood pressure.",
   "start": 94.92,
   "end": 98.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay do you snore?",
   "start": 98.72,
   "end": 99.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "My wife Danny Ellis says I snore like a chainsaw. She says sometimes I stop breathing and then gasp.",
   "start": 100.36,
   "end": 106.46
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'm tired most days too. That's important, I'll come back to it. Any medicines over the counter, decongestants, pain relievers.",
   "start": 106.94,
   "end": 115.84
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I take pseudoephedrine most mornings for my sinuses, 30 milligrams, maybe two tablets.",
   "start": 116.66,
   "end": 122.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Alcohol smoking.",
   "start": 123.98,
   "end": 124.56
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Three or four beers on the weekend, I've never smoked. I'm a project manager at Brightwater Construction so I eat a lot of fast",
   "start": 125.38,
   "end": 133.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "food on the road if I'm being honest. Thanks for being straight with me. Let me check you. Your blood pressure is 148 over 94 in the right arm, 144 over 90 in the left. I repeated it after five minutes and got 146 over 92. Pulse 80. Weight is 228 pounds, which puts your BMI at 31 .4. No brutes in your neck or belly. Heart is regular, no murmurs. Lungs are clear, no legs swelling, and the pulses in your groin and feet are normal.",
   "start": 133.18,
   "end": 168.66
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay.",
   "start": 169.4,
   "end": 169.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I also looked at the labs and ECG doctor. Linkvist sent. Kidney function is normal. Create 9 1 .0, potassium 4 .1, and ura 1c is 5 .6, so no diabetes. The ECG from August shows sinus rhythm with some voltage that suggests the heart muscle may be a little thick from the pressure.",
   "start": 170.5,
   "end": 193.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thick is that bad?",
   "start": 194.16,
   "end": 194.8
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "It's a sign the blood pressure has been working the heart harder and it's very treatable. So my thinking is this. You have high blood pressure that isn't controlled yet. To be clear,",
   "start": 195.34,
   "end": 205.94
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "you haven't had a heart attack or a stroke,",
   "start": 206.3,
   "end": 208.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "those were your parents. But your family history does raise your risk, so we want to get your numbers down and look at the whole picture.",
   "start": 208.8,
   "end": 216.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, that helps.",
   "start": 217.22,
   "end": 218.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "First, I'm increasing the amlodipine to 10 mg once a day. Second, please stop the pseudoephedrine, it pushes the blood pressure up. Use a fluticasone nasal spray instead, two sprays in each nostril once a day.",
   "start": 218.06,
   "end": 233.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 36,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I didn't know that about the decongestant.",
   "start": 234.36,
   "end": 236.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 37,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Most people don't. Third, the snoring and stopping breathing sound like sleep apnea, which is a common cause of hard to control blood pressure. I'm ordering a home sleep study. I also want an echocardiogram to look at the heart muscle and a fasting lipid panel and a urine test for protein.",
   "start": 237.12,
   "end": 256.44
  },
  {
   "idx": 38,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay. On the lifestyle side, try to",
   "start": 257.11,
   "end": 260.69
  },
  {
   "idx": 39,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "keep salt under 2000 mg a day and cut back to no more than one or two beers at a time. Keep checking your blood pressure at home twice a day and bring the log in your cuff next time.",
   "start": 260.69,
   "end": 272.81
  },
  {
   "idx": 40,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "We'll do, should I worry about chest pain like my dad?",
   "start": 272.81,
   "end": 276.15
  },
  {
   "idx": 41,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "If you ever get chest pain, sudden weakness, or trouble speaking, call 911 right away. Otherwise I'll see you back in four weeks to go over the tests and your home numbers.",
   "start": 276.85,
   "end": 288.53
  },
  {
   "idx": 42,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Sounds good, thanks doctor.",
   "start": 289.53,
   "end": 290.71
  }
 ],
